{"sessions":[{"sessionId":"603b50b3-f6c2-4de4-b17d-aebb1ae33b81","narrative":"Completed ticket #38 on `build/scope-drift` and committed the implementation; a ticket comment was posted. The new third Retro-eye signal evaluates whether work performed by a registered ticket session matches the ticket’s stated scope, reusing the existing git scan, worktree-to-parent attribution, evidence limits, GitHub seam, composition, and tracker paths rather than adding another watcher or brain tier.

False positives are constrained both in the model prompt and in `decideDrift`: drift requires two affirmative booleans plus an articulated explanation; ambiguous or insufficient ticket scope produces silence. The implementation also catches thrown `Brain` errors, converts them to audited silence, and reliably releases the cap slot.

Validation passed: all eight drift cases, the live Luna test in both in-scope and drift directions, recursive schema-required coverage, TypeScript checking, and the full suite (`571` passed, `2` skipped, `0` failed). The scenario was registered in `all-scenarios.ts` and chained through registry slot 2 after rebasing concurrent main changes. The branch was not merged, the ticket remains open, and main/other worktrees were untouched.","summary":"Ticket #38 scope-drift implementation is complete, committed, fully green, and awaiting merge with the ticket still open.","status":"done"}]}

{"sessions":[{"sessionId":"603b50b3-f6c2-4de4-b17d-aebb1ae33b81","narrative":"Completed ticket #38 on `build/scope-drift` and committed the implementation, then posted a ticket comment. The new Retro-eye signal compares the diff covered by a registered ticket session against that ticket’s stated scope, reusing the existing git scan, worktree-to-parent attribution, evidence limits, GitHub seam, composition, and tracker paths rather than adding another watcher or model tier.

The implementation deliberately favors silence over false positives: the prompt documents the burden of proof, safe cases, ambiguity policy, and cost asymmetry; `decideDrift` additionally requires both boolean findings plus an articulated explanation. Tickets with too little stated scope never reach the brain. It also now catches thrown `Brain` errors, degrading them to audited silence and releasing the cap slot on every path; this was added red-test-first.

All eight drift cases passed. The live Luna test exercised the real `buildDriftPrompt` in both directions, accepting an in-scope refactor while flagging billing webhooks as drift. Recursive schema tests enforce that every object’s `required` fields exactly match its properties. After rebasing over concurrent changes, both scenarios were registered in `CONTRIBUTED[2]` and chained through `registry.get(2)`. Final verification passed with `bun x tsc --noEmit` and `bun test` reporting 571 passed, 2 skipped, and 0 failed. The branch was not merged; the ticket remains open, and main plus other worktrees were untouched.","summary":"Ticket #38 is implemented, committed, commented, and fully green on `build/scope-drift`, but intentionally not merged and still open.","status":"done"}]}

{"sessions":[{"sessionId":"603b50b3-f6c2-4de4-b17d-aebb1ae33b81","narrative":"The scope-drift slice progressed from the red-test phase for `decideDrift` through completion of ticket #38 on `build/scope-drift`. The implementation adds a third Retro-eye signal that compares a registered ticket session’s actual diff with its stated ticket scope, reusing the existing git scan, `gh` seam, evidence limits, brain, composition, and tracker paths. Its conservative false-positive policy is encoded in both the prompt and `decideDrift`: drift requires two affirmative booleans plus an explanation, while ambiguity or insufficient scope produces audited silence.

Validation passed with TypeScript clean and 571 tests passing, 2 skipped, and none failing. A live Luna test correctly classified both an in-scope refactor and an out-of-scope billing-webhook change, and recursive schema coverage protects the required/properties invariant. The work also hardened the watcher against thrown `Brain` errors and ensured cap slots are released on every path. After rebasing over concurrent changes, both scenarios were registered in `all-scenarios.ts`. The branch was committed and the ticket updated, but deliberately not merged; main and other worktrees were untouched.","summary":"Ticket #38 is implemented, committed, fully validated, and ready for review or merge on `build/scope-drift`.","status":"done"},{"sessionId":"0a3ac707-b3db-412d-9744-0260a0ba08ff","narrative":"The build reached 17 of 18 completed tickets: #35’s curator pass closed, leaving only #36, the v1 live acceptance run. Its headless worker was initially healthy and executing with a brief preloaded from already-verified facts. The remaining acceptance proof then encountered a local tooling prerequisite: cmux is still at 0.62.2, while one of the ten scenarios requires version 0.64.22 or newer.

Human action is now required: fully quit cmux with ⌘Q, reopen it, click the installed-update banner if it remains, and confirm `cmux version` reports at least 0.64.22. Once upgraded, the dispatcher is expected to detect the version, close #15, and dispatch #7 automatically while preserving the running loop.","summary":"The final v1 acceptance work is blocked until cmux is manually restarted and upgraded to version 0.64.22 or newer.","status":"blocked"}]}

{"sessions":[{"sessionId":"603b50b3-f6c2-4de4-b17d-aebb1ae33b81","narrative":"All 8 drift cases passed, followed by a green retro suite and typecheck. The session specified Slice 10 / §14, including the false-positive stance.

Ticket #38 was built and committed on `build/scope-drift`, with a tracker comment posted. It adds the third Retro-eye signal: checking whether a registered ticket session’s diff matches the ticket’s stated scope. It reuses existing git attribution, evidence caps, the `gh` seam (including closed tickets), and compose/tracker filing—without adding a watcher, brain, or model tier.

False positives are addressed in both the prompt and `decideDrift`: drift requires two booleans plus articulated prose; ambiguous or unmeasurable scope remains silent. `Brain` exceptions now degrade to audited silence and release the cap slot. The live-luna test passed both in-scope and drift cases, and schema tests enforce matching `required` and `properties` keys. Current-main gates are green: `bun x tsc --noEmit` passed and `bun test` reported 571 pass, 2 skip, 0 fail. The branch was not merged; the ticket remains open and main was left untouched.","summary":"Ticket #38 is implemented and committed with all tests green, but remains unmerged with the ticket open.","status":"done"}]}
